    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/logicSummary> "Definition of administrative action";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/premiseText> "(2) Administrative action is:  (a) making a decision under subsection 484F(5) or (6); or  (b) making a decision under subsection 484G(4), (6) or (7); or  (c) giving a notice under subsection 484F(8) or 484G(8); or  (d) doing, or refusing or failing to do, anything related to making a decision under subsection 484F(5) or (6) or 484G(4), (6) or (7). The ACMA is treated as having taken administrative action";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/executionSurface> "modalities::logic::deontic";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/confidence> 1.0000;
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/curationStatus> <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/Proposed>.
<https://ns.webcivics.net/concept/telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484j-ss-3> a <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/Concept>;
